WEBVTT

00:00:09.051 --> 00:00:15.283
The analysis is done and the checks pass. To keep a record or have it reviewed, write a report

00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:19.432
Select the Analysis, menu Solve → Report (parts library)

00:00:19.432 --> 00:00:25.536
Report language: Chinese or English (same numbers, different text)

00:00:25.536 --> 00:00:31.583
The report number comes from your quality system and may be left empty; here we fill one in

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:38.133
Revision A, reason “first issue”: keep the defaults, OK

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:48.633
It asks whether AI should write “interpretation and advice”: the numbers are filled in by the program and AI never decides pass/fail. No AI in this lesson: No

00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:55.811
The report is written: a Word file, plus a PDF because LibreOffice is installed

00:00:55.811 --> 00:01:03.107
Let's open it. Page 1: summary — max stress, safety factor, trust; below, the part and material (with sources)

00:01:03.107 --> 00:01:11.307
Constraints, loads, steps; then mesh and trust checks: max stress and displacement on three mesh levels, a verdict for each

00:01:11.307 --> 00:01:15.642
Results: stress and displacement plots

00:01:15.642 --> 00:01:23.632
No AI explanation, so that section is empty; then limitations and a review checklist — check item by item before signing

00:01:23.632 --> 00:01:28.632
Finally traceability: program versions, file fingerprints, revision history

00:01:28.632 --> 00:01:35.600
Reports are a Pro feature; the free edition computes and shows results and checks
